{"step_index":1958,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T17:36:28Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-23T13:36:28-04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-08-23T13:36:32-04:00\nThe search for \"Google Gemini API current active models 2025 2026 gemini-2.5-flash gemini-2.0-flash\" returned the following summary:\nAs of August 2026, the Gemini API model landscape has evolved significantly beyond the 2.0 and 2.5 generations[1][2]. Below is the current status of the models you inquired about and the broader Gemini ecosystem.\n\n### Status of Requested Models\n*   **Gemini 2.0 Flash:** This model is **deprecated and has been shut down** (as of June 1, 2026)[3].\n*   **Gemini 2.5 Flash:** This remains an **active and available** model[4][5]. It is widely used as a high-performance \"workhorse\" model that balances speed, cost, and intelligence, often featuring built-in \"thinking\" capabilities for complex tasks[4][6][7].\n\n### Current Gemini API Ecosystem (August 2026)\nThe current lineup is primarily focused on the **Gemini 3, 3.1, 3.5, 3.6, and 3.7** generations[1][5][2]. Key active models include:\n\n*   **Gemini 3.7 Flash:** Recently released (August 13, 2026) and generally available[8][9]. It is currently positioned as one of the most intelligent \"Flash\" models, optimized for coding and agentic workflows[8][5].\n*   **Gemini 3.6 Flash:** An active model optimized for complex, multi-step workflows and improved multimodal reasoning[5].\n*   **Gemini 3.5 Flash:** A highly capable model delivering Pro-level performance at Flash-tier speeds and pricing[5].\n*   **Gemini 3.1 Pro:** The flagship high-capability model, prioritized for advanced reasoning, complex coding, and deep-thinking tasks[10][1][11].\n*   **Flash-Lite variants:** Several versions (e.g., **Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite**) exist for high-throughput, cost-sensitive, and latency-sensitive tasks[10][5].\n\n### Summary Table\n| Model Generation | Status | Primary Use Case |\n| :--- | :--- | :---